  "result": "**Bulk discount feature complete!** \u2705\n\n**What's been implemented:**\n\n1. **src/totals.js** \u2014 Added bulk discount logic:\n   - `lineBulkDiscount(line)` \u2014 Calculates 2.5% extra discount for lines with qty \u2265 10, applied after the line's own discount\n   - Modified `lineVAT()` \u2014 Now applies both line discount and bulk discount before calculating VAT\n   - Modified `invoiceTotals()` \u2014 Includes both discounts in the total discount field\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Re-exports:\n   - Added `lineBulkDiscount` to re-exports for backward compatibility\n\n3. **test/totals.test.js** \u2014 20 comprehensive bulk discount tests:\n   - Threshold validation (qty 9 vs 10)\n   - Bulk discount calculation (2.5% on amount after line discount)\n   - VAT after both discounts\n   - Invoice totals with bulk discount\n   - Multiple lines with mixed bulk eligibility\n   - Edge cases and rounding\n\n4. **Test updates**:\n   - Updated render tests to reflect new totals with bulk discount\n   - Updated invoices tests to use qty < 10 when not testing bulk discount\n   - All 466 tests pass (426 existing + 40 new bulk/totals tests)\n\n**How it works:**\n```\nLine with 10+ units:\n- Line total = qty \u00d7 unitPrice\n- Line discount = lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent%\n- After line discount = lineTotal - lineDiscount\n- Bulk discount = (After line discount) \u00d7 2.5%  \u2190 NEW\n- Final amount = After line discount - bulkDiscount\n- VAT = Final amount \u00d7 vatRate%\n```\n\nExample: 10 units \u00d7 \u20ac100, 10% line discount, 21% VAT:\n- Line total: \u20ac1000\n- Line discount (10%): \u20ac100 \u2192 \u20ac900 remaining\n- **Bulk discount (2.5% of \u20ac900): \u20ac22.50** \u2192 \u20ac877.50 remaining\n- VAT (21%): \u20ac184.28\n- Total: \u20ac1000 - \u20ac100 - \u20ac22.50 + \u20ac184.28 = \u20ac1,061.78\n\nReady to commit when approved.",
